{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1333567-asset-skills","id":1333567,"title":"Asset Skills","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-09-01T11:26:40-07:00","id":1333567,"title":"Asset Skills","content":"Search isn\u2019t giving me a way to just search this forum so apologies if this isn\u2019t a new question:<br /> <br /> What\u2019s an asset skill? What makes those skills you get from your pantheon asset skills rather than just the skills you get from your pantheon path?<br /> <br /> In Hero it says the your guide grants asset skills. It specifically says you don\u2019t get a +1 in them. Why is that necessary to say? I see nothing in Origin (the core rules) about asset skills granting a +1.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24935-werlynn","name":"werlynn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-01T12:07:58-07:00","id":1333576,"title":"","content":"Asset Skills are just ways to say Skills linked to something, in these cases Paths or Guides.<br /> <br /> Path Asset Skills are those three skills linked to your Path. In Chargen, they allocate your Skill spread depending on the Path's rank to you.<br /> <br /> Guide Asset Skills don't grant you improvements to your Skill rank, which is why they establish that so you don't go thinking that you get points in those Skills for having a Guide. Instead, your Guide Asset Skills determine which Skills you can use the Guide's Stunt with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","us